      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Some impressive last start winners come together. PRIORY PARK (1) is the one that appeals most after returning from a 24-week break with a stunning win over 1000m at Kembla. Failed at his only try over 1200m but it was in Saturday company at the end of the prep. McDonald a key booking. Can go right on with it. REGAL (6) started at $1.90 and justified the quote over this distance at Kembla last time out, lengthening beautifully to win her maiden by seven lengths. Has only raced twice so her potential is untapped. BAYLIE'S FOLLY (5) returned for a second campaign with a very comfortable maiden win over today's journey in a recent Nowra maiden. Yet to be testing on anything but a wet track which is the only small question mark. KOSEI TOP (2) has not raced since winning a Sale maiden over this trip back in July. Takes on better types now but has plenty of scope for improvement this prep. LETTERS PATENT (3) has had two solid trials leading up to this return. Should give a good account.",
